+*   **Input:** Ray starting point, ray vector (to next resample location), original volume dataset (voxel values), density Lookup Table (LUT).
+*   **Output:** Resampled density values, X and Y gradient components for the rotated dataset.
 
-**Data Structures:**
-*   **Weight Memory:** Size $256\text{K} \times 16$ bits. Stores precalculated interpolation weights. Addressed by three 6-bit fractional parts (one per coordinate: $u, v, w$) of the resampling location [S1].
-*   **Gradient Buffer:** Limits the maximal resampled dataset size to $512^3$ [S1].
-*   **Memory System:** Supports conflict-free access to 8 neighbor voxels. Uses Fast Page Mode, alternate memory bank read-out, and a 1-entry cache for previously used voxels. A controller returns 0 for addresses outside the data cube [S1].
-*   **Data Precision:** 16-bit for density and gradient values [S1].
