-2.  **Address Generation:** Use hardware to generate sampling point positions. Round the $X, Y, Z$ components of the sampling location to obtain integer addresses of the 8 neighbor voxels in the original dataset [S1].
-3.  **Density Mapping:** Map the raw voxel values to density values using the density LUT. This allows for grey-value segmentation without prior data segmentation [S1].
-4.  **Weight Lookup:** Retrieve interpolation weights from the Weight Memory using the three 6-bit fractional parts of the sampling location coordinates [S1].
-5.  **Interpolation (Backward Mapping):** Perform weighted interpolation among the 8 voxel neighbors to compute the resampled density value. The weights support filters such as tri-linear interpolation or a local approximation of $\text{sinc}(x)$ [S1].
-6.  **Gradient Estimation:** Estimate the $X$ and $Y$ components of the gradient using 20 Sobel filters applied to the interpolated data [S1].
